NCT00490139_33765513,"Disease-Free Survival (DFS) at the Primary Analysis [Time Frame: From randomization until the date of the first occurrence of disease recurrence, a contralateral invasive breast cancer, a second primary cancer, or death from any cause (median follow-up of 4.5 years)]","At a median follow-up of 6.9 years, 705 DFS events for L+T versus T were observed. Hazard Ratio (HR) for DFS was 0.86 (95% CI, 0.74-1.00) for L+T versus T and 0.93 (95% CI, 0.81-1.08) for T→L versus T. The 6-year DFS were 85%, 84%, and 82% for L+T, T→L, and T, respectively. HR for OS was 0.86 (95% CI, 0.70-1.06) for L+T versus T and 0.88 (95% CI, 0.71-1.08) for T→L versus T. The 6-year OS were 93%, 92%, and 91% for L+T, T→L, and T, respectively. Subset analyses showed a numerically better HR for DFS in favour of L+T versus T for the hormone-receptor-negative [HR 0.80 (95% CI, 0.64-1.00; 6-yr DFS% = 84% versus 80%)] and the sequential chemotherapy [HR 0.83 (95% CI, 0.69-1.00; 6-yr DFS% = 83% versus79%)] subgroups.",0.6649,33.51,llm,gpt-4o-mini,concordant,"The registered primary outcome is Disease-Free Survival (DFS) at the Primary Analysis with a median follow-up of 4.5 years, while the publication reports DFS at a median follow-up of 6.9 years, indicating a change in the timeframe of the primary endpoint. Guardrail applied: Endpoint 1: an attribute was marked different without affirmative evidence.",low,False,True,False,False,,0.35,Concordant (no change),modified,Disease-Free Survival (DFS) at a median follow-up of 6.9 years,,True,Endpoint 1: an attribute was marked different without affirmative evidence.,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Disease-Free Survival (DFS) at the Primary Analysis"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Disease-Free Survival (DFS) at a median follow-up of 6.9 years"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": false, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additi