NCT01982448_32798689,"Number of Participants With Pathologic Response by HR-deficiency (HRD) Status [Time Frame: Evaluated after definitive breast surgery, up to 4-5 months from enrollment.]","One hundred and thirty-nine patients were evaluable for response, including 88 (63.3%) who had surgery at 12 weeks and 51 (36.7%) who crossed over to an alternative provider-selected preoperative chemotherapy regimen due to inadequate clinical response. HRD results were available for 104 tumors (74.8%) and 74 (71.1%) were HRD positive. The RCB-0/1 rate was 26.4% with cisplatin and 22.3% with paclitaxel. No significant association was observed between HRD score and RCB response to either cisplatin [odds ratio (OR) for RCB-0/1 if HRD positive 2.22 (95% CI: 0.39-23.68)] or paclitaxel [OR for RCB-0/1 if HRD positive 0.90 (95% CI: 0.19-4.95)]. There was no evidence of an interaction between HRD and pathologic response to chemotherapy.",0.6738,32.62,llm,gpt-4o-mini,concordant,"The registered primary outcome focused on pathologic response by HR-deficiency status, while the published primary outcome reported the RCB-0/1 rate, which is a different construct. There is no evidence that the registered primary outcome was reported in the publication. Only the current registry entry is available, and it does not provide evidence of any prior registered outcomes. Guardrail applied: Endpoint 1: a construct change was asserted without affirmative evidence.",low,False,True,False,False,,0.35,Concordant (no change),different,RCB-0/1 rate,,False,Endpoint 1: a construct change was asserted without affirmative evidence.,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Number of Participants With Pathologic Response by HR-deficiency (HRD) Status"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""RCB-0/1 rate"", ""same_construct"": false, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": false, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": fa